  "body": "The existing six interacting cyclic-inverse shears use a valid uniform\namplification bound. Tracking each array's chronological dependencies reduces\nthe sufficient shared coarse/working precision from 86/145 to 69/112 bits at\nmargin 1/2, and from 151/291 to 117/226 bits at margin 1/16, for the complete\n12-stage forward/inverse word and 40 target bits. The rounded leaf, source\nrestoration and all execution calls remain unchanged.\n\nThe package gives the standard componentwise-majorant proof specialized to\nthis interface, exact pins and an immutable selected snapshot, 20 actual source\nfixture replays with exact restoration, 144 dense oracle prefix comparisons,\nan independent 4,680-word / 279,616-corner check, and 13 mathematical/package\ncontrols. All three commands in the README pass under isolated optimized\nPython 3.14.5; relocation in a path with spaces passes.\n\nThese are sufficient numerical budgets, not a measured speedup, arbitrary\ndirty-bit restoration, fixed-tape invoice, supplier admission or new kappa.\nThe source's clean low-bit capacity, phase/coefficient preparation and compiler\nobligations remain. Only `research/word-precision53/` is added. Credit Chafik\nBoukhalfa's source implementation and composition proof, Ali Romman's inverse\nbound, and the PR628 lineage. Prepared for @woklerx with substantial OpenAI\nCodex assistance; Apache-2.0.\n\nConcurrent PR1085 by Hanson Sun (@bbMisk) sharpens ideal prefix coefficients\nfor PR905/628's balanced dirty commutator recursion. This package treats the\nfixed six cubic-inverse shears and their full inverse word with componentwise\nmagnitude/error propagation. It imports neither PR1085 code nor its savings.\n",
